MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The Breeze feels like a natural next choice after Old Sock because I want more Clapton, especially the relaxed blues feel of JJ Cale's songs.",
    "Step Back connects with my interest in Hendrix and Clapton through expressive blues guitar, while Hypnotic Eye makes sense given my recent interest in Benmont Tench."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Shadows in the Night misses what I want today because traditional vocal standards do not offer the bluesy singing and guitar that draw me in.",
    "The Endless River's atmospheric instrumental sound is less appealing right now, and CSNY 1974 asks for more listening time than I want to give a large live collection."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "Recognizing familiar rock artists seems to count too much when their recommended album has a very different sound from what I want.",
    "A broad connection to roots music seems to be treated as enough, even though country, live collections, and guitar-driven blues appeal to me differently today."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The combination of bluesy vocals and expressive guitar matters more to me right now than a loose connection to familiar artists.",
    "Finding an album appealing does not mean I would choose it today; I would act on the strong Clapton and Johnny Winter connections and leave the other possibilities for later."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations understand my interest in blues and roots rock, but sometimes stretch that interest beyond the specific sound and strong connections that would make me choose an album today."
}
